  "ethos:attribution": "Solar resource data (c) 2019 Solargis. PV power potential data (c) 2019 Solargis. Air temperature data (c) 2019 ECMWF, NASA and Solargis. Terrain elevation derived from SRTM, viewfinderpanoramas.org, GEBCO by Solargis, 2018. (c) The World Bank, Source: Global Solar Atlas 2.0. Data obtained from the Global Solar Atlas, a free, web-based application developed and operated by Solargis s.r.o. on behalf of the World Bank Group, utilizing Solargis data, with funding provided by the Energy Sector Management Assistance Program (ESMAP).",
  "ethos:license_status": "resolved",
  "ethos:coverage_note": "Holds the world layers published for Global Solar Atlas 2.0 in 2019-09 (ELE, OPTA, TEMP, monthly PVOUT) and 2020-09 (GHI, DNI, DIF, GTI), each as a GeoTIFF with its PDF poster map and ISO 19139 .xml metadata. Grids: 9 arcsec (about 250 m) for GHI, DNI, DIF and GTI; 30 arcsec (about 1 km) for TEMP, ELE and the twelve monthly PVOUT layers; 2 arcmin (about 4 km) for OPTA. Extent 180W-180E and 55S-60N: nothing north of 60N or south of 55S. Data period 1994/1999/2007 (depending on the region) to 2018.\nTHIS IS NOT GLOBAL SOLAR ATLAS 2.5, although the source directory on the cluster is called global_solar_atlas_v2.5. The files say data to 2018, and the release notes date the extension of the data period to 2020 to GSA 2.5 (June 2021). What is held is the database introduced with GSA 2.0, which releases 2.1 to 2.4 kept. Air temperature is the ECMWF/NASA/Solargis product of that time, not the ERA5 and ERA5-Land blend introduced with GSA 2.11 (May 2024).",
  "ethos:retrieved": "unknown",
  "ethos:origin": "downloaded",
